<p>NOTE: United Dental Care Inc's results for the six months of 1997 include a $2.3 million charge relating to reviewing accounting and increased accounts receivable reserves.</p>
<p>The company put the non-recurring charge, which it previously estimated at $1.5 million, to be $2.3 million for the six months of 1997 to include a re-engineering project.</p>
<p>The company will file restated financial statements for the first quarter ended March 31 to include $2 million of the charge.</p>
<p>The restatement will result in after-tax income of $1.5 million, or $0.16 a share, in the first quarter, compared with an after-tax income of $2.7 million, or $0.30 a share, previously reported.</p>
